=== PARITY (vs web components/charts/TimeMarker.tsx) ===
  The web source is a thin wrapper over a Recharts `<ReferenceLine>` that marks an alert's
  moment on whatever time chart the drill-through page (`useAlertContext()`) already shows,
  and renders nothing when `x` is absent. The native parity keeps that exact data + logic
  while promoting it to a full shared surface (the prompt's state envelope).
  Data sources (web → native P1/S8 source seam):
    useAlertContext (drill-through alert) → TimeMarkerSource → TimeMarkerUpdate
                                            (alert | nil, loading/loaded/failed, live/stale/offline)
  Verbatim web logic ported + unit-pinned:
    normalizeSeverity(s): nil/'' → info · warning → warn · error/fatal → critical ·
      ok/success → success · info/warn/critical → self · else info (lowercased) ·
    marker severity = normalizeSeverity(severity ?? 'warn') ·
    SEVERITY_STROKE = { info:#0ea5e9, warn:#f59e0b, critical:#ef4444, success:#10b981 } ·
    x == null || x === '' → render nothing (→ empty state) ·
    label ?? 'Alert' · strokeWidth ?? 2 · strokeDasharray default solid.
  Recharts → Swift Charts mapping:
    `<ReferenceLine x stroke strokeWidth strokeDasharray label{value,position:'top',fill}>`
      → `TimeMarkerRuleMark: ChartContent` = vertical `RuleMark(x:)` + `.foregroundStyle`
        (exact severity hex) + `.lineStyle(width/dash)` + `.annotation(position:.top)` chip ·
    reusable as a `ChartContent` so any host `Chart{}` composes it (the web reuse pattern) ·
    `export { severityTokens }` → public `TimeMarkerSeverity.color/softTint/borderTint`.
  States (all render, never a blank box): loading(skeleton rail) · empty(web `x==null` →
    "No alert selected") · error(+retry) · stale(chip + one auto-refresh) · offline(cached +
    chip) — a freshness envelope (ADR-013) around the web marker-vs-nothing split.
  i18n: the web source has no `t()` calls (anonymous; one hardcoded 'Alert'); that maps to
    `timeMarker.defaultLabel`, and all native chrome/severity/a11y resolve via the P1/S10
    facade (catalog carries the English). a11y: chart VoiceOver label + spoken marker /
    empty summary (severity + label + moment); Dynamic Type via Font.TS; reduce-motion-safe.
  Telemetry: emits view.opened with surface slug "TimeMarker" once (P1/S11), asserted.

